# PROJECT: Gold Loan SaaS for Indian Pawnbrokers

## STACK (do not deviate)
- Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript strict mode
- Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- Supabase (Postgres + Auth + Storage) via @supabase/supabase-js v2 and @supabase/ssr
- TanStack Query v5 for server state
- React Hook Form + Zod for forms
- Vercel hosting
- No custom backend server. Supabase is the backend.

## HARD RULES (violating these breaks the product)
1. Every table has a `shop_id` column. Every query filters by `shop_id`. No exceptions.
2. Row Level Security (RLS) is enabled on EVERY table. Never disable it.
3. Money is stored as Postgres `numeric`. Never `float`, never `real`.
4. Due dates are Postgres `date`. Event timestamps are `timestamptz`.
5. `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` is server-only. Never prefix with `NEXT_PUBLIC_`. Never import in client components.
6. `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` is the only key allowed in client code.
7. Interest rate is FROZEN on the loan row at creation. Never recalculate rate later.
8. Phone numbers stored as `+91XXXXXXXXXX` (strip spaces, no dashes).
9. WhatsApp uses `wa.me` click-to-chat links. No WhatsApp Business API in MVP.
10. Borrower NEVER logs in. Borrower access is via magic-link token at `/p/[token]`.

